-- The trailing byte is exactly what the `.prefix` CID-boundary assumption admits.
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x26, 0x00, 0x01, 0x71, 0x12, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∈ language .drislCidPrefix := by decide +kernel

/-! ### Link rules: `(multihash code, digest length)` pairs -/

/-- A custom profile with SHA-256 at two digest lengths (32, and truncated to 16 bytes). Not a
published profile: it shows that the pair set, not the hash function, fixes the length. -/
def sha256TwoLengths : Profile := ⟨true, false, .exact, ⟨[0x55, 0x71], [(0x12, 32), (0x12, 16)]⟩⟩

-- BLAKE3 (`1E`) with a 32-byte digest: BDASL, not DASL, not ATProto.
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x25, 0x00, 0x01, 0x55, 0x1E, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∈ language .drislBdaslExactCid := by decide +kernel
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x25, 0x00, 0x01, 0x55, 0x1E, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∉ language .drislExactCid := by decide +kernel
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x25, 0x00, 0x01, 0x55, 0x1E, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∉ language .atprotoCoreExactCid := by decide +kernel
-- SHA-256 is still allowed under BDASL.
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x25, 0x00, 0x01, 0x71, 0x12, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∈ language .drislBdaslExactCid := by decide +kernel
-- A declared length that does not match the digest: `20` (32) declared, 31 bytes present.
-- Rejected under both boundaries (under `.prefix` there are fewer bytes than declared).
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x24, 0x00, 0x01, 0x71, 0x12, 0x20, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∉ language .drislExactCid := by decide +kernel
