-- The same algorithm at another length: SHA-256 declared and present at 31 bytes is not an
-- allowed pair in DRISL.
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x58, 0x24, 0x00, 0x01, 0x71, 0x12, 0x1F, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∉ language .drislExactCid := by decide +kernel
-- With the pair `(12, 16)` listed, a 16-byte SHA-256 digest is allowed, and the 32-byte one
-- still is; DRISL rejects the 16-byte one.
example : [0xD8, 0x2A, 0x55, 0x00, 0x01, 0x71, 0x12, 0x10, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00] ∈ language sha256TwoLengths := by decide +kernel
